{"name":"Volute","hex":"#445a5e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"volute","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The characteristic spiral curve on an Ionic capital, widely copied in other styles and in neoclassical architecture.","The spirals or whorls on a gastropod's shell."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a spring: having a spiral curve on its tail.","Rolled up in any way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/volute"}],"entries":[{"title":"Volute","blocks":[{"text":"A volute is a spiral, scroll-like ornament that forms the basis of the Ionic order, found in the capital of the Ionic column. It was later incorporated into Corinthian order and Composite column capitals. Four are normally to be found on an Ionic capital, eight on Composite capitals and smaller versions on the Corinthian capital."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/SixIonicOrders.jpg/330px-SixIonicOrders.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volute"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/%E5%BA%93%E5%BA%93%E7%89%B9%E5%B0%BC%E9%99%B6%E7%A2%97%E9%99%B6%E7%BD%90.JPG/960px-%E5%BA%93%E5%BA%93%E7%89%B9%E5%B0%BC%E9%99%B6%E7%A2%97%E9%99%B6%E7%BD%90.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/%E5%BA%93%E5%BA%93%E7%89%B9%E5%B0%BC%E9%99%B6%E7%A2%97%E9%99%B6%E7%BD%90.JPG/1280px-%E5%BA%93%E5%BA%93%E7%89%B9%E5%B0%BC%E9%99%B6%E7%A2%97%E9%99%B6%E7%BD%90.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/%E5%BA%93%E5%BA%93%E7%89%B9%E5%B0%BC%E9%99%B6%E7%A2%97%E9%99%B6%E7%BD%90.JPG/960px-%E5%BA%93%E5%BA%93%E7%89%B9%E5%B0%BC%E9%99%B6%E7%A2%97%E9%99%B6%E7%BD%90.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","li